xt.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@17\"}]}]]}]\n18:[]\n10:\"$W18\"\n11:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"children\":\"$L1a\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L1b\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$16\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$L1c\"}]}]}],null]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0_novvjei_gxi.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n1d:Tb49,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Vintage & Old-Fashioned Animal Names: 100+ Timeless Ideas 🕰️\",\"description\":\"Classic never goes out of style. Discover charming vintage animal names from the Victorian era through the 1950s that bring timeless elegance to your pet.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-17\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-06\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/vintage-and-old-fashioned-animal-names/\"},\"wordCount\":149,\"articleBody\":\" Everything old becomes new again — including pet names. Vintage and old-fashioned names carry dignity, nostalgia, and timeless charm. A cat named Agatha or a dog named Winston feels instantly distinguished and cultured. This guide explores the most charming retro names organized by era. Victorian Era Names (1837-1901) Victorian names carry maximum vintage charm: <strong>Agatha</strong>, <strong>Beatrice</strong>, <strong>Clarence</strong>, <strong>Dorothy</strong>, <strong>Edmund</strong>, <strong>Florence</strong>, <strong>Gertrude</strong>, <strong>Harold</strong>, <strong>Imogen</strong>, <strong>Jasper</strong>, <strong>Mabel</strong>, <strong>Percy</strong>, <strong>Rufus</strong>, <strong>Walter</strong>. Edwardian & 1920s Names The Jazz Age brought flair: <strong>Arthur</strong>, <strong>Daisy</strong>, <strong>Evelyn</strong>, <strong>Frank</strong>, <strong>Gladys</strong>, <strong>Hazel</strong>, <strong>Irene</strong>, <strong>Leonard</strong>, <strong>Myrtle</strong>, <strong>Pearl</strong>, <strong>Stanley</strong>, <strong>Vera</strong>, <strong>Wilfred</strong>. Mid-Century Names (1930s-1950s) The Greatest Generation names: <strong>Betty</strong>, <strong>Clifford</strong>, <strong>Doris</strong>, <strong>Eugene</strong>, <strong>Gloria</strong>, <strong>Herbert</strong>, <strong>Joyce</strong>, <strong>Lloyd</strong>, <strong>Marilyn</strong>, <strong>Norman</strong>, <strong>Phyllis</strong>, <strong>Shirley</strong>, <strong>Vernon</strong>. Vintage Literary Names Explore our name generators for {african-golden-wolf}, {airedale-terrier}, {andean-cock-of-the-rock}, {amur-leopard}, and {aldabra-giant-tortoise} to find the perfect name for your companion. Literature offers timeless names: <strong>Atticus</strong>, <strong>Darcy</strong>, <strong>Estella</strong>, <strong>Fitzgerald</strong>, <strong>Gatsby</strong>, <strong>Heathcliff</strong>, <strong>Josephine</strong>, <strong>Ophelia</strong>, <strong>Pip</strong>, <strong>Scout</strong>, <strong>Tess</strong>, <strong>Wuthering</strong>.\",\"image\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/images/og/blog-vintage-and-old-fashioned-animal-names.png\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"}14:[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$1d\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"FAQPage\\\",\\\"mainEntity\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Why are vintage pet names trending?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Vintage names feel warm, nostalgic, and distinguished. T